4782 cikkáṇa 'slippery, unctuous' MBh., cikkiṇa - lex., cikvaṇa - 'stuck to' Yaś. [See cikka -²] Pk. cikkaṇa -, °kiṇa - 'sticky, oily, thick'; Gy. eur. čiken 'fat, butter', pal. čúkna 'oil'; S. cikaṇi f. 'mud';
P. cīkuṇā , cīkṇā , ciknā 'sticky, oily, smooth'; A. sikaṇ 'fine, smooth and excellent, plump'; B. cikan 'smooth,
glossy, fine, thin'; Or. cikaṇa , °ṇā 'oil, ghee'; Bi. ciknā 'oil seeds in general', (Gaya) 'ghee'; Mth. cĭ̄kan 'slippery, polished', Bhoj. cīkan ; Aw. lakh. cīkan 'smooth'; H. ciknā 'oily, fat, rich, smooth'; OG. cīkaṇauṁ 'sticky', G. cikṇũ , M. cikaṇ , Ko. cikkaṇa . cikkā- see chikkā -. cikkira- see cikka -¹. * cikkhalla- 'mud' see cikhalla -. cikvaṇa- see cikkáṇa -.
